{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1168699-need-help-designing-relic-for-my-vtr-chronicle","id":1168699,"title":"Need help designing relic for my VtR chronicle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-18T18:50:42-08:00","id":1168699,"title":"Need help designing relic for my VtR chronicle","content":"I had plan for the chronicle to be more social and politic oriented (more of a sandbox style) but when given the opportunities in Elysium to further their ambition and gain recognition as a group, my players kinda froze for a minute. Now nothing wrong with that, the game is set at the end of the week and i know that one of my player has been doing a lot of unpaid overtime. <br /> As subtly as i could, i devised a new plan for the characters that would be more straightforward for the players. Then as they gain more recognition, i'll gently guide the player toward more political and social situations. <br /> So instead the characters were asked to help a semi-important (who wants to upgrade their statut to very-important) member of the kindred community. The tasks at hand are straightforward relic hunting. So now i kind of need help figuring out interesting relics.<br /> <br /> Context of the chronicle:<br /> The chronicle is set in Venice and it is currently in 1207. I plan for the relics together to somehow starts or help propagate the plague of 1348 that wiped about half the population of Venice. <br /> So far the only idea i have is a mirror that shows the water of the canals as blood in the reflection. But i am a bit swamped with school stuff and i cant seem to find ideas for other relics.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the help.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T20:26:07-08:00","id":1168711,"title":"","content":"A flute that, when played, summons a swarm of rats (the fleas on these rats are vectors for the bubonic plague) Playing the notes in a certain pattern allows the user to command and control them as if they have a limited form of Animalism 1 and 3. After a set amount of time the rats &quot;disappear&quot;. And within 24 hours after that several children in the town/domain where the flute was played disappear. (They'll be transformed as rats and among the next summoned swarm of rats.) <br /> <br /> A bouquet of posies that never appear to wilt. In the hands of a kindred they gain the appearance and benefits of the blush of life. Even low Humanity Vampires don't look like corpses. In the hands of a human or ghoul they are immune to disease and any symptoms but they can become vectors.<br /> <br /> Black dog statue. The statue comes to life each morning and tracks and kills as many cats as it can in a 6 hour period then returns home and goes inert. When rising that evening, the owner (determined by an esoteric ritual that involves willpower expenditure) gets a number of vitae equal to the number of cats killed by the statue that day. The dog statue owner instantly knows where the vitae comes from and how it is obtained. The owner can also command the statue to animate at night and function as a well trained dog. (Yes it can work for ghouls if they invest willpower to claim ownership.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.ancient-origins.net/myths-legends/disturbing-true-story-pied-piper-hamelin-001969\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.ancient-origins.net/myths...hamelin-001969</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 12-19-2017, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T09:51:32-08:00","id":1168825,"title":"","content":"Crusaders sacked Constantinople just three years ago (1204), facilitated by the Venice merchant lords who among other things wanted unfettered access to ports and trading posts in the Black Sea/Eastern Med. At the moment the Latin Quarter is set up and the crusaders are in charge. Now is when various &quot;things&quot; that were in Constantinople, safe, for hundreds of years if not millennia are making their way to collectors and enthusiasts across the Mediterranean.<br /> <br /> Some of these things the world would be better off for, were they never to see the light of day again.<br /> <br /> Among such are a series of unusual Icons, created during the latter reign of Justinian, depicting the effects and perhaps causes (metaphysical and physical) of the Plague of Justinian of the 540s AD. There are four icons: ranging in size from a minuscule about the size of a human hand, painted in details with eyelash-hair brushes, to a fresco of irregular pieces that was broken up during the Iconoclast controversy and stored in a series of heavily-sealed crates with only a letter describing how it looked assembled. The whereabouts of half the letter is known; the other half was last seen [redacted]. In-between in size are one icon in an enclosed cabinet, beautifully decorated in gold and precious stones, and a stone pillar about half again the size of a man and ending in a kind of Egyptian point--like a rounded obelisk. The obelisk was plastered with a painted and embroidered silk scene, which may have been removed to avoid its destruction. In each icon, the Virgin Mary appears, overlooking the suffering; the Virgin appears very much, in fact, like the Empress Theodora.<br /> <br /> The four icons correspond to the four outbreaks of the plague during the 6th century, and it was this plague that provided the first known major, apocalyptic introduction of Y. Pestis to Europe. Even the Emperor Justinian contracted the plague, but he got better... only, not really. In his latter years chronicles complain that he and his queen, Theodora, would detach their heads and fly around the palace, drinking blood. Things got weird, and it was Theodora herself who commissioned the Icons. She may still be out there, somewhere, with our without her imperial husband, carrying on her own Requiem. She might even be willing to help sufficiently dedicated, subservient and foolish Kindred decipher the clues in the Icons, the tiny writing lined in a proprietary mix of pigments and Mordus Vitae, and to understand how the Icons join together to properly depict a ritual of power murderous enough to bring an empire to its knees and its unliving masters to beg for mercy at <i>any</i> cost.<br /> <br /> <br /> This help? I leave Googling the references here to you.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":". 12-19-2017, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T13:49:22-08:00","id":1168908,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the silence, i had a busy day. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1168699-need-help-designing-relic-for-my-vtr-chronicle?p=1168825#post1168825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This help?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>It help tremendously thank you. I've done a ton of research on Venice and the sack of constantinople, but this makes me want to deepen my research on constantinople itself. <br /> I have to ask, did you just make that on the spot, cause what you describe feels very ... alive (thats not the right word ... vivid maybe?). Anyway i find that very impressive and will surely use it in my chronicle. Thank you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1168699-need-help-designing-relic-for-my-vtr-chronicle?p=1168711#post1168711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A flute that, when played, summons a swarm of rats (the fleas on these rats are vectors for the bubonic plague) Playing the notes in a certain pattern allows the user to command and control them as if they have a limited form of Animalism 1 and 3. After a set amount of time the rats &quot;disappear&quot;. And within 24 hours after that several children in the town/domain where the flute was played disappear. (They'll be transformed as rats and among the next summoned swarm of rats.)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.ancient-origins.net/myths-legends/disturbing-true-story-pied-piper-hamelin-001969\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.ancient-origins.net/myths...hamelin-001969</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Thats interesting, a bit after the sack of constantinople, there was the construction of the <i>Fontego dei Tedeschi</i> that served as the headquarters for the german merchants in Venice. I can see a heist situation where the characters have to infiltrate the <i>Fontego</i> and steal the flute. <br /> Maybe, i'll have the flute belong to a visiting dignitary from the emperor of the invictus (i think thats a thing at that point in time? I'll have to reread the covenant book to be sure.)<br /> Thank you<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T05:55:01-08:00","id":1169060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1168699-need-help-designing-relic-for-my-vtr-chronicle?p=1168908#post1168908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for the silence, i had a busy day. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It help tremendously thank you. I've done a ton of research on Venice and the sack of constantinople, but this makes me want to deepen my research on constantinople itself.<br /> I have to ask, did you just make that on the spot, cause what you describe feels very ... alive (thats not the right word ... vivid maybe?). Anyway i find that very impressive and will surely use it in my chronicle. Thank you.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It was made on the spot. Though, I've done research on 6th-9th century Byzantine history for my own campaign, which will eventually get there if all works out. I like to note historical oddities that speak to the Darkness peeking through and staining history. In this case the bits about demonic Justinian and Theodora are 100% legit (to the written record, biased as it may be), as are the four major outbreaks of the plague (which they think started from grain shipments through Alexandria in Egypt--a Mekhet or Morbus connection perhaps, or Theban sorcery?), and the Iconoclast controversy and swings.<br /> <br /> For the CofD I theorize that the icons had, by then, taken on a wholly unwholesome connection to spirits and sorcery, which some wanted to stamp out and others found... useful.<br /> <br /> Theodora is a historical force of nature. The woman deserves an NPC spot in any Dark Era vamp game, as does Belisarius--who probably would have succeeded in conquering the formerly Roman empire for Byzantium if he hadn't been slowed by the plague and politics (his wife Antonina was a favorite of Theodora and regarded as a sorceress/enchantress). I'd probably use Theodora as interested in avenging Constantinople by unleashing hell on Venice, and Belisarius as a more honorable, moderate figure indisposed to vengeance.<br /> <br /> I'll probably use this idea as well, or at least set it up as a thing.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T10:25:40-08:00","id":1169125,"title":"","content":"Can I recommend that if you create and use multiple relics that one of them be the exact opposite of the others, a key to prevent or even undue some of the damage the others caused.<br /> Think of this as the Good-Guy relic created to save the day, the final treasure desperately sought by those who don't want the city to fall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T10:30:40-08:00","id":1172680,"title":"","content":"Here are two examples from, even though I'm probably late for the party.<br /> <br /> A flute of mouldy wood that makes no sound whatsoever. But the truth is that when playing this flute anyone who would hear it had it been a normal flute gets the plague.<br /> <br /> A mirror that shows, when looking at it from an angle, the pathway down into the underworld and through which one can communicate, with, or at least get the attention from, certain of its inhabitants. Probably of Etruscan origin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}